{
  "id": 21,
  "name": "v12_regret_boost",
  "intent": "Strengthen the regret backbone (0.06→0.18) and trim the nearest_remaining penalty (0.12→0.08) to directly target uniform underperformance, where the previous cluster_density bonus alone was insufficient. Keep a slightly softened return-aware ramp and a modest cd term to preserve clustered/grid behavior. Hypothesis: explicit regret lookahead dominates on structureless uniform instances by resolving lookalike candidates, while a lighter nr penalty avoids over-centrality bias that can harm diversification mid-tour.",
  "tags": [
    "regret",
    "return_aware"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    rd = f['return_distance']\n    nr = f['nearest_remaining']\n    r = f['regret']\n    p = f['progress']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    return -d + 0.22 * rd * (1 + 0.5 * p) + 0.18 * r - 0.08 * nr + 0.03 * cd",
